# Command: SDD Migrate

Command: /sdd-migrate
Mode: READ_WRITE
Purpose: Run pending migrations after .sdd/ schema updates

Description:
  Executes pending migrations for the active project instance.
  Migrations are applied in order and tracked in migrations/ state.
  This command MUST be run after any .sdd/ update that changes
  file locations, schemas, or project structure.

  Shared registries (projects/prompts/) are validated but not migrated
  as project instances — they have their own migration rules.

Usage:
  /sdd-migrate
  /sdd-migrate --list
  /sdd-migrate --apply=<migration-id>
  /sdd-migrate --rollback=<migration-id>

Options:
  --list              List pending and applied migrations
  --apply=<id>        Apply specific migration by ID
  --rollback=<id>     Rollback specific migration by ID
  --dry-run           Show what would be migrated without changing files

Migration Location:
  .sdd/projects/example_project/migrations/
    INDEX.sdd              — Migration registry and state
    001-project-separation.sdd  — Move project/ state to projects/example_project/
    002-path-references.sdd     — Update path references after restructuring
    003-schema-updates.sdd      — Schema version updates
    004-prompts-registry.sdd    — Validate prompts/ shared registry

   Shared registries (validated but not migrated as instances):
     .sdd/projects/prompts/     — Formalized prompt registry

  New system directories (created fresh, no migration needed):
     .sdd/features/             — Feature planning and layer assignment

Migration Registry:
  {
    "project": "example_project",
    "applied": [
      {
        "id": "001-project-separation",
        "applied_at": "2026-08-29T08:00:00Z",
        "description": "Move concrete project state from project/ to projects/example_project/"
      }
    ],
    "pending": [],
    "schema_version": "1.0.0"
  }

Exit Codes:
  0 - Migrations applied successfully
  1 - Migration failed
  2 - No pending migrations
  3 - Migration already applied

State: +
